Package: gis2shiny
Title: Turn GIS Vector Data into Interactive Shiny Applications
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person('David', 'Amakye', role = c('aut', 'cre'), email = 'amakyekojodavid@gmail.com')
Description: Creates interactive 'Shiny' applications from simple features
    objects and vector GIS files in Shapefile, GeoJSON, and GeoPackage formats.
    Explore features on a map, filter their attributes, view tables and
    summaries, and download selected data. Export an editable 'Shiny'
    application with its spatial data for local use or deployment.
URL: https://github.com/david-amakye/gis2shiny
BugReports: https://github.com/david-amakye/gis2shiny/issues
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
Imports:
    sf,
    shiny,
    leaflet,
    htmlwidgets,
    DT,
    htmltools
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
